    <briefdescription>
<para>C++20 concept satisfied when <computeroutput>T</computeroutput> provides <computeroutput>begin()</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>end()</computeroutput> only as functions found by argument-dependent lookup. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type to be checked.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
The <computeroutput>free_range</computeroutput> concept is satisfied when <computeroutput>T</computeroutput> has no <computeroutput>begin()</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>end()</computeroutput> members (see <computeroutput>container_like</computeroutput>), but calls of <computeroutput>begin()</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>end()</computeroutput> with a <computeroutput>const T&amp;</computeroutput> argument are valid and return an iterator and its sentinel, as in a range-based <computeroutput>for</computeroutput> statement, which then uses them. </para>
